FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with the patches listed before it in recipes/core/base/recipe.toml applied. ihdad's shared ring belongs to the playback handle that opened it: the caller receives a descriptor of its own while the driver keeps the one it maps, and closing that handle unmaps the ring and unlinks its shm object. Each ring gets its own object name, a second ring while one exists is refused with EBUSY, and block writes wait while a ring feeds the output. ipcd's shm scheme lets a directory handle unlink the objects under its own prefix, which the driver needs inside the null namespace.

